            {
                "entry_id": "d2f97a66-1db4-3dc1-a2ff-2e11d785ba8d",
                "word": "solutionnisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3e8a3a77-085d-4e2e-92ea-6f035ce499b0",
                        "entry_id": "d2f97a66-1db4-3dc1-a2ff-2e11d785ba8d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "solutionnismes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71054af6-476d-309a-b4da-c154b64a62c3",
                        "entry_id": "d2f97a66-1db4-3dc1-a2ff-2e11d785ba8d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Façon de voir ou d’espérer la solution à des problèmes comme des problèmes sociaux ou écologiques uniquement grâce à la technique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "89d071cc-3105-47ed-87d4-1c2a1ee4200a",
                                "sense_id": "71054af6-476d-309a-b4da-c154b64a62c3",
                                "text": "Pendant le confinement, le solutionnisme a gagné en crédibilité : télétravail, enseignement à distance, vidéo à la demande, etc."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cbb9c90c-4403-4463-add6-46e36d1e2544",
                        "source_entry_id": "d2f97a66-1db4-3dc1-a2ff-2e11d785ba8d",
                        "source_sense_id": "71054af6-476d-309a-b4da-c154b64a62c3",
                        "target_lang_word": "solutionism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "solutionism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be30b9e0-c1f6-3b8d-a5f0-bd9661f1f8b4",
                                        "entry_id": "e789a914-7780-3eb1-b54d-cb2a877dd56f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The belief that all difficulties have benign solutions, often of a technocratic nature."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "223e171d-a3e4-438d-8770-2cb5029493b7",
                                                "sense_id": "be30b9e0-c1f6-3b8d-a5f0-bd9661f1f8b4",
                                                "text": "Solutionism is just a belief that for every problem there exists a solution; and successful persons are those who solve problems."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aade0a82-e282-4969-ad38-159181ef0f43",
                                                "sense_id": "be30b9e0-c1f6-3b8d-a5f0-bd9661f1f8b4",
                                                "text": "So before we can embark on discussing the shortcomings of solutionism in areas like politics or crime prevention, it's worth getting a better grasp of the pernicious intellectual influence of Internet-centrism—a task we turn to in the next chapter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "925fede6-a144-47fd-a063-60b67286ed69",
                                                "sense_id": "be30b9e0-c1f6-3b8d-a5f0-bd9661f1f8b4",
                                                "text": "Evgeny Morozov defines this trend as solutionism: a normal problem-solving apparatus gone into overdrive (Morozov 2013). Thanks to ICTs, Morozov claims, new types of solutions that weren't possible a few years ago are now ready at hand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "131f8cc8-6938-3835-8bcb-d72510e15b53",
                                        "entry_id": "e789a914-7780-3eb1-b54d-cb2a877dd56f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The providing of a solution or solutions to a customer or client (sometimes before a problem has been identified)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
